# PINNED 2026-08-07. This repo is the PUBLIC proof (github.com/ACNoonan/exceedance-design-effect);
# exceedance-paper is the private workspace behind it. Every private lane reaches the shared
# instrument by symlink into ~/Documents/research-vocab/, and this repo must not: that path exists
# only on one machine, so the link would dangle for anyone who clones the repo. A vendored copy is
# what makes the artifact self-contained and re-runnable by a stranger.
#
# Not the closed-lane case. The three calibrated-uncertainty pins are frozen because their copy IS
# the provenance record for numbers already reported. This one is frozen because of who the reader
# is. It SHOULD track the canonical over time — it just has to be refreshed deliberately rather
# than by a link that updates silently.
#
# Pinned at sha256 29de96547ac2057e… — byte-identical to the canonical on 2026-08-07.
#
# To refresh (a deliberate act, not a sync):
#   cp ~/Documents/research-vocab/verdict.py .
#   re-run the claim scripts, diff their committed <claim>_RESULTS.txt
#   update the sha above
# A refresh that changes a published number is a correction, and gets recorded as one.
verdict.py: public artifact repo — must be self-contained; a symlink into ~/Documents would dangle for anyone who clones it

